  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 has strict reporting timelines but only covers confirmed incidents. S2 sets a 55°C test and a 5% review threshold, but exceeding it does not automatically stop sales; per-model results go to customers and regulators, not the public. S3 and S4 require new-unit shut-off and suppression with 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression deadlines. S5 keeps the 8/100k trigger but allows open-ended corrective action instead of mandatory recall, and notices are only 'promptly'."
